<title>USA: US corporate debt avalanche triggered by low rates.</title>
<headline>US corporate debt avalanche triggered by low rates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corporate underwriters are getting set to launch an avalanche of new issues as lower intrest rates continue to lure U.S. corporations into the debt arena, dealers said.</p>
<p>Currently, the 30-year U.S. Treasury bond is up 17/32 at 100-30/32 driving the yield sharply lower to 6.43 percent. &quot;If this keeps up we'll see a ton of new issues in the market,&quot; one high-grade syndicate source said.</p>
<p>Dealers expect the pace to heat up substantially before the holidays when desks traditionally are thinly staffed.</p>
</text>
